      "claims": [
        {
          "text": "Linear determines is_sliced by comparing its padded local dimensions with full_in_features and full_out_features. Its default alignment of 128 rounds dimensions upward; it is not a slice-count threshold.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_0c83d1331ee2407d93c6f472f022d1a9"]
        },
        {
          "text": "GatedMLP builds gate/up slices along output features and down slices along input features, preserving full dimensions and offsets. Alternate keys let these sliced modules load the original unsliced checkpoint tensors. Loading a selected MLP slice directly loads its gate, up and down linears.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_f7d5bd53cc3b4e688342a41b9d9b96b3"]
        },
        {
          "text": "With padding disabled for sliced loads, LinearFP16 receives the transposed full weight on CPU. It slices dimensions that match the declared full dimensions, slices bias alongside output columns, copies the selected weight into independent storage, and then the existing unswap_cpu path transfers it to the requested device. This is not partial file I/O: the loader still reads the complete tensor.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_286a242cc5f44b679662f0b48bd08438", "call_0c83d1331ee2407d93c6f472f022d1a9", "call_ea5b8081f9a54f6789da70cfbf0b090a", "call_0f908f8c675745d2b05d3d608208012a"]
